    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>Dorian Adams gracefully ceded leadership of Clan Ventrue and withdrew from city politics the moment Marcus Vitel arrived, retiring to the fortified, gargoyle-crowned Castle Adams in the Maryland countryside. A 5th-generation elder Embraced in 1701, Adams affects the theatrical mannerisms of a cinematic vampire &mdash; sweeping capes, a hammy Romanian accent &mdash; as camouflage for genuine paranoia and genuine danger; his castle's secret corridors, security systems, and magical traps have swallowed entire Sabbat war parties without a trace. Adams alone among Washington's elders has correctly deduced that Marcus Vitel is secretly Lasombra, and has quietly begun cooperating with the Inconnu.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>Play the harmless old ham to the hilt &mdash; capes, accent, theater &mdash; while missing absolutely nothing. You know the Prince's secret and it terrifies you more than any Sabbat war party ever has.</p>",
    "notes": "Correctly suspects Marcus Vitel is secretly Lasombra; quietly cooperating with the Inconnu. Retired to fortified Castle Adams in Maryland.",
    "npcType": "vampire"
  },
